{"path":"types/numeric_limits/is_iec559","title":"std::numeric_limits<T>::is_iec559","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::numeric_limits&lt;T&gt;::</span>is_iec559","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/is_iec559","section":"types","kind":"page","summary":"The value of std::numeric_limits<T>::is_iec559 is true for all floating-point types T which fulfill the requirements of IEC 559 (IEEE 754) standard.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n</tbody>\n<tbody class=\"t-dcl-rev\">\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx11\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> is_iec559<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx11\">(until C++11)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> is_iec559<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_iec559</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> for all floating-point types <code>T</code> which fulfill the requirements of IEC 559 (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IEEE_754-2008\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">IEEE 754</a>) standard. If <c